# Operations {id="nm-ops"}

::summary{id="nm-ops-summary"}
How to build, verify, release, and run Noma. The authoritative sources are
`CLAUDE.md` (commands, release flow), `package.json` (scripts),
`.github/workflows/` (CI gates), `docs/noma-cloud.noma` (Cloud config), and
`docs/runbooks/cloud-launch.md` (production checklist). This page is the
short version.
::

## Dev setup {id="nm-ops-dev-setup"}

Requires Node 20 or newer (`package.json` `engines`). Python 3 is needed
only for the Python SDK and seed tests. Chromium (via Puppeteer) is needed
for PDF output and the browser UI tests.

```bash
npm install
npx puppeteer browsers install chrome            # PDFs + UI tests
python3 -m pip install -e 'packages/agent-sdk-py[test]'   # optional

npm run noma -- check examples/research-thesis.noma
npm run noma -- render examples/agent-plan.noma --to html --out dist/agent-plan.html
npm run cloud:dev                                 # Cloud from source (tsx)
```

Run a production-like Cloud locally:

```bash
npm run build:cloud
PORT=3000 npm start          # node dist/cloud-server.js
curl http://localhost:3000/healthz
```

Then open `http://localhost:3000/cloud.html` (`docs/noma-cloud.noma`, "Run it locally").

## Verification gates {id="nm-ops-gates"}

`CLAUDE.md` says a feature is not done until **all** of these pass:

```bash
npx tsc --noEmit
npm test
npm run build:site
```

| Gate | Command | Runs in |
|---|---|---|
| Typecheck (core) | `npx tsc --noEmit` | `ci.yml`, `pages.yml` |
| Typecheck (browser) | `npm run typecheck:web` | `ci.yml` |
| Lint | `npm run lint` | `ci.yml`, `pages.yml` |
| Unit and integration tests (`test/*.test.ts`, node:test) | `npm test` | `ci.yml`, `pages.yml` |
| Conformance corpus | `npm run verify:conformance` | `ci.yml`, `pages.yml` |
| Memory/doc drift | `npm run check:memory` | `ci.yml`, `pages.yml` |
| Version lockstep | `npm run release -- check` | `ci.yml`, `pages.yml` |
| Package smoke, agent SDK, MCP, LSP, Python | `smoke:package`, `test:agent-sdk`, `test:mcp`, `test:lsp`, `test:python-sdk`, `test:python-seed` | `ci.yml` |
| Examples and docs render | `render:examples`, `render:docs` | `ci.yml` |
| Full site incl. PDFs | `npm run build:site` | `pages.yml` |
| Everything at once | `npm run test:full` | local, `release.yml` |

::callout{tone="info"}
Known sandbox failure: `test/cloud-ui.test.ts` asserts no console errors
and fails where an external font request is blocked by a proxy. It passes
on CI runners (`docs/status-2026-09-25.md` §6).
::

`.github/workflows/freshness.yml` runs a scheduled docs staleness check.

## Release process {id="nm-ops-release"}

Bump every versioned location together (`CLAUDE.md` "Versioned Locations"):
`package.json` (and workspace packages), `docs/spec.noma` frontmatter and
"(vN)" headings, `docs/agent-protocol.noma` `version:`, a new
`CHANGELOG.md` heading, the `README.md` status paragraph, and a new
`PLAN.md` §24 subsection. `npm run release -- check` catches drift.

There are three paths into `.github/workflows/release.yml`; all run the full
gate before tagging or publishing:

| Path | How | When to use |
|---|---|---|
| Merge a release PR | Push to `main` where `package.json`'s version has no `v<version>` tag: the workflow tags, publishes to npm, and creates the GitHub release | Default since v0.19.0; works from Claude Code cloud sessions |
| Local tag | `git tag vN.N.N && git push origin vN.N.N` after pushing `main` | Manual releases |
| Manual dispatch | Run `release.yml` with `tag=vN.N.N` | When neither of the above is possible |

Release runs share a concurrency group, so two paths for the same version
never both tag. After publishing, close shipped issues and verify the npm
packages, GitHub release, MCP registry descriptor, and GitHub Pages
(`docs/runbooks/npm-publish.md`, `docs/runbooks/mcp-registry-publish.md`).

GitHub Pages: `pages.yml` builds `dist/` on every push to `main` and
publishes the docs site.

## Deploying Noma Cloud {id="nm-ops-deploy"}

| Option | What | Reference |
|---|---|---|
| Docker image | `Dockerfile`: two-stage `node:20-bookworm-slim`, runs `node dist/cloud-server.js` on port 3000, data under `/data/noma`, `HEALTHCHECK` on `/healthz`, stops on `SIGTERM` | `Dockerfile` |
| ezkeel | `ezkeel.yaml` (`name: noma-cloud`, `port: 3000`); `npm run deploy:ezkeel:dry-run`, then `npm run deploy:ezkeel`; roll back with `ezkeel rollback noma-cloud` | `docs/runbooks/cloud-launch.md` |
| Home mini PC (dogfooding) | Self-hosted kit for the one-space-per-project dogfood instance | `deploy/minipc/` (being written; read its README) |
| AWS/EU reference | CloudFormation template, validated but never deployed | `infra/`, `docs/enterprise.noma` |
| Static site only | `npm run deploy:hetzner` pushes the built `dist/` to a static host | `scripts/deploy-hetzner.sh` |

Production rules from `docs/runbooks/cloud-launch.md`:

- Serve over HTTPS only. Session and CSRF cookies are `Secure` on every host except `localhost`. Forward `X-Forwarded-Proto: https` from the proxy.
- Set `NOMA_CLOUD_ADMIN_USER_IDS`. Without it, production `/api/enterprise` routes fail closed with `403 admin_not_configured`.
- Mount `/data/noma` on persistent storage and watch free space (SQLite, WAL, revisions, audit records grow).
- Run the 13-step staging smoke test before go-live.

Background work (webhook deliveries, mail outbox, SIEM shipping, Slack
outbox) runs on an in-process timer; the standalone worker is
`apps/worker/cloud-queue.ts`.

## Backups {id="nm-ops-backups"}

From `docs/runbooks/cloud-launch.md`, "Backup and restore":

- On ezkeel: `ezkeel backup <app>`.
- Direct host: use SQLite's online backup, or stop the service first. Never copy only the main database file while a WAL is live.
- Keep: the SQLite backup, deterministic `.noma` export bundles, the secret files (stored separately), the image digest and Git commit, and the date of the last restore rehearsal.
- Attachment blobs live under `<storage root>/blobs` unless `NOMA_CLOUD_BLOB_STORE=s3`; back them up with the database.
- Wiki spaces synced to Git (`noma cloud sync`) have a second copy in each repo's `wiki/` directory, but that does not cover chat, Work, comments, or audit data.

## Environment variables that matter {id="nm-ops-env"}

Full lists are in `docs/noma-cloud.noma`. Prefer `*_FILE` variants for
secrets.

| Variable | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `NODE_ENV`, `PORT` | `production`, `3000` |
| `NOMA_CLOUD_DATA_DIR`, `NOMA_CLOUD_DB` | Document dir and SQLite path (image defaults under `/data/noma`) |
| `NOMA_PUBLIC_DIR` | Built static assets (`/app/dist` in the image) |
| `NOMA_CLOUD_ACCESS_TOKEN_FILE`, `NOMA_CLOUD_INVITATION_CODE_FILE` | The two required production secrets |
| `NOMA_CLOUD_ADMIN_USER_IDS` | Workspace admins (required in production) |
| `NOMA_CLOUD_PUBLIC_URL` | Public base URL used in links |
| `NOMA_CLOUD_TRUST_PROXY` | `1` only behind a proxy that overwrites forwarded headers |
| `NOMA_CLOUD_OIDC_ISSUER`, `_CLIENT_ID`, `_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE`, `_REDIRECT_URL` | Native OIDC login |
| `NOMA_CLOUD_BLOB_STORE` | `s3` for S3-compatible attachment storage |
| `NOMA_CLOUD_LLM_PROVIDER`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | Generative AI and hosted agents (`anthropic`, `fake`, `none`) |
| `NOMA_CLOUD_EMBEDDINGS`, `NOMA_CLOUD_EMBEDDINGS_URL`, `_MODEL`, `_API_KEY_FILE` | Real embeddings for search |
| `NOMA_CLOUD_EZKEEL_URL`, `NOMA_CLOUD_EZKEEL_TOKEN_FILE` | `/deploy` and `/test` runs on ezkeel |
| `NOMA_CLOUD_SLACK_BOT_TOKEN`, `NOMA_CLOUD_SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET` | Two-way Slack bridge |
| `NOMA_CLOUD_SIEM_URL`, `NOMA_CLOUD_SIEM_TOKEN_FILE` | Audit NDJSON forwarding |
| `NOMA_CLOUD_SMTP_URL`, `NOMA_CLOUD_MAIL_FROM` | Email notifications and digests |
| `NOMA_CLOUD_URL`, `NOMA_CLOUD_TOKEN` | Client side: `noma cloud export-space` / `noma cloud sync` |

::callout{tone="warning"}
Never put secret values in this wiki, in a `.noma` page, or in chat. DLP
(`/api/enterprise/dlp`) catches common token shapes, but it is pattern-based
and not a guarantee (`docs/enterprise.noma`).
::
